From 099278782a49b5f3b2639073ebcf3b1dedb1ba76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominick Morales <dmorales2024@my.fit.edu>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:01:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] accel/kvm: add the VM introspection object

-object introspection,id=kvmi,chardev=<socket chardev> connects to an
introspection tool (e.g. LibVMI over libkvmi), does the kvmi-v7
handshake and passes the socket to KVM with KVM_INTROSPECTION_HOOK.
KVM then talks to the tool directly. Unhooks on disconnect, reset and
shutdown; reconnects through the chardev's reconnect-ms.

Forward-ported from the KVM-VMI kvmi-v7 QEMU (4.2.1) without remote
memory mapping and suspend/migration interception.
---
 accel/kvm/meson.build |   1 +
 accel/kvm/vmi.c       | 574 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 qapi/qom.json         |  24 ++
 3 files changed, 599 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 accel/kvm/vmi.c

diff --git a/accel/kvm/meson.build b/accel/kvm/meson.build
index 397a1fe1..bcc9727c 100644
--- a/accel/kvm/meson.build
+++ b/accel/kvm/meson.build
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@ kvm_ss = ss.source_set()
 kvm_ss.add(files(
   'kvm-all.c',
